B.L_=new A.fS(2,"FROM THE DESK DRAWER \u2014 LOG OF R. HALLORAN, NIGHT OPERATOR","Whoever is reading this: the rundown is a lie, the quotas are real. Keep the needle up. It does not care what you broadcast, only that you are broadcasting.")
B.KY=new A.fS(3,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 214","Eight of them. There have only ever been eight. I have a key for each and I have never needed a ninth, which I used to find comforting.")
B.KW=new A.fS(4,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 341","They have started arriving in the order I think of them in. I have stopped keeping the list in order.")
B.KZ=new A.fS(5,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 508","The window in the booth does not open and has never opened. Whatever is in the field is not getting in that way. I want to be clear that this is the only reassuring sentence in this book.")
B.KX=new A.fS(6,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 720","Slept four hours in the chair with the carrier up. Woke to find the log open at a page I had not written yet. The handwriting is mine.")
B.KV=new A.fS(7,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 901","It is not trying to get out. I have had this backwards for two years. It is trying to get me to stop, which is a different thing, and it is much more patient about it.")
B.KU=new A.fS(8,"HALLORAN \u2014 NIGHT 1,114","There is a second operator on the roster now. I have not met them. I have not been told their name. The roster is in my handwriting.")
B.KT=new A.fS(9,"HALLORAN \u2014 FINAL ENTRY","If you are new: it is not the noise. It is the quiet after the noise, when you have got it right and you are sitting there being pleased with yourself. That is when it looks at you properly.")
B.L0=new A.fS(10,"STATION MEMO \u2014 UNSIGNED","R. HALLORAN did not sign off on the morning of the 1,115th night. The carrier was up. The chair was warm. The log was open to a blank page, and the page is the one you have been writing on.")
B.Ie=s([B.L_,B.KY,B.KW,B.KZ,B.KX,B.KV,B.KU,B.KT,B.L0],A.a7("w<fS>"))
